Part of epic #40 ("Style the website with CSS"). Establishes the site's visual style guide — a soft, bubbly, bright/airy look driven by reference mockups (gradient background, pill-shaped controls, rounded display font) — starting with the shared layout and the home page as a combined first pass, since home page styling depends on the tokens defined for the shared layout.

## Step 1: Shared Layout
### Status
Complete

### GitHub Issue
#41

### Summary
Apply the new visual style (gradient background, font pairing, pill-shaped nav/buttons/inputs) to the shared layout — navbar and footer chrome — without changing nav items, text, links, or structure.

### Motivation
Sub-issue of epic #40. Establishes the reusable token layer (STYLE_GUIDE.md + CSS custom properties) that later per-page styling issues (#42–#49) will build on.

### Proposed Changes
- Add STYLE_GUIDE.md documenting palette/type/shape rationale and usage guidance (no literal values — points to site.css).
- Add CSS custom properties in site.css :root: --gradient-page, --color-accent-yellow, --color-accent-blue, --color-accent-green, --color-text-on-gradient, --radius-pill, --font-display, --font-body.
- Load Cherry Bomb One and Quicksand webfonts.
- Apply --gradient-page as the body background sitewide via _Layout.cshtml.
- Restyle navbar to transparent background with pill-shaped, white-outlined nav links — same nav items/routes/text as today.
- Restyle footer to transparent background, white text, centered — same copy as today.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Gradient background renders behind every page via the shared layout.
- Navbar/footer visual style matches reference mockups; no nav item, link, or text changed.
- Cherry Bomb One and Quicksand are loaded and exposed as --font-display/--font-body.
- STYLE_GUIDE.md exists and documents the tokens without duplicating their literal values.

### Out of Scope
- Hover/focus/active/disabled states.
- Styling beyond shared layout + home page.
- The dark outer "frame" from the mockups (confirmed to be mockup/artboard framing, not real UI).

---

## Step 2: Home Page
### Status
Complete

### GitHub Issue
#42

### Summary
Apply the Step 1 tokens to Home/Index.cshtml (Create Event / Join Event) to match the reference mockups.

### Motivation
Sub-issue of epic #40. Home/Index.cshtml already structurally matches the mockups, so this is a styling-only pass; doing it alongside Step 1 gives a concrete working example of the new style guide.

### Proposed Changes
- Style "CREATE A NEW EVENT" / "JOIN AN EVENT" headings with --font-display.
- Restyle Event Name input as a pill with --color-accent-yellow fill/border.
- Restyle Event Code input as a pill with --color-accent-blue fill/border.
- Restyle GO! buttons as small circular buttons using --color-accent-green.
- No changes to form markup structure, validation, or controller logic.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Home page visually matches the reference mockups' shapes/colors/fonts for these elements.
- Existing form behavior/validation is unaffected.

### Out of Scope
- Hover/focus/disabled states.
- Other pages.

### Dependencies
Step 1 (consumes the tokens defined there).
